    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4586" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurŭla</span></b> , ae, f.
		dim.
		aura, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				gentle breeze;</i> trop. (in eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">famae aurula,</span>”
				<i>a puff of fame</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 28</span></i>
			 (an imitation of Vergil's tenuis famae aura, A. 7, 646): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Graecarum litterarum,</span>”
				<i>a whiff of</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 34</span></i>
			.</div>
